{
  "id": "UP03Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Cystourethroscopy / ureteroscopy",
  "description": "A cystourethroscopy or ureteroscopy visualizes the inside of your bladder and urethra (or ureters) using a thin camera passed through the urethra. This outpatient procedure can be purely diagnostic or therapeutic, depending on your condition. The camera shows your doctor exactly what's causing symptoms like bleeding, pain, or obstruction. If needed, small instruments can remove stones, destroy tumors, remove tissue samples, or place stents. The procedure takes 15-90 minutes depending on complexity. You may have mild burning with urination for a few days. Most people go home the same day. The cost of this procedure may vary depending on the complexity involved. Categories include diagnostic, therapeutic, simple, therapeutic, complex, with ureteroscopy, and with implant.",
